/-!
# Nonregular symplectic modularity lifting: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned APIs whenever their carriers can be expressed
with a few elementary definitions on native objects.

Regular ordinary unitary finiteness and selected symplectic support are inputs
from OrdinaryAutomorphicFormsAndModularityLiftingPartII §§4.7–4.8 (p=2) and
§§6.3–6.4 (p>2), respectively; the singular support application remains §11.4.

No headline theorem is statable at the pins. The missing carriers are:
* Integral normalized Siegel p-actions (§1.1), secondary Hasse geometry
  (§3.1a), and corrected scalar/vector theta and injectivity (§4.2) lack
  integral genus-two moduli, automorphic coefficients and differential operators.
* All-degree coherent interpolation and qualified crystalline specialization
  (§2.3–4) lack Siegel coherent eigensystems and crystalline-period functors.
* Ordinary weight-two symplectic interpolation, its pure monodromy upgrade,
  dual-spin overconvergent interpolation and completed isotypy (§2.5–8) lack
  automorphic local parameters, reductive pseudocharacters and higher-Coleman
  completed eigenspaces.
* Regular Hecke-valued representations (§3.4), the two cuspidal Hasse-projection
  injections (§4.8), and the singular minimal deformation (§5.2) lack actual
  integral coherent Hecke images, geometric Hasse maps and local deformation data.
* Finite-coefficient Klingen comparison (§6.4) lacks compactified Klingen covers,
  automorphic coefficients and their pullback/trace maps.
* Selected balance (§7.4), minimal R=T with positive cuspidal freeness (§8.2–3),
  and classical CG modularity (§8.5) lack the selected coherent module, its
  integral p-idempotent, the universal symplectic deformation ring and Siegel forms.
* Variable-weight ordinary R=T and control (§9.2), ordinary p-adic modularity
  (§9.3), and parallel parabolic lifting (§9.4) lack Siegel Hida families and
  their universal ordinary deformation rings.
* Characteristic-zero local freeness (§10.7), multiplicity one over residue fields
  at regular points (§11.3), component support and four-chamber rank one (§11.4–5), and classical
  weight-two modularity lifting (§11.6) lack the actual four higher-Hida modules,
  their arithmetic specialization, Hecke support and higher-Coleman comparison.

-/

